{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-57006","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65293","text":"Runefort Protocol — v0.1"}]},{"id":"blk-57007","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65294","marks":["bold"],"text":"A layout protocol for living, file-backed, tile-grid web apps."}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57009","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65295","marks":["bold"],"text":"Part of the [&] Protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-65296","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-65297","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/ECOSYSTEM.md"}],"text":"Ecosystem overview"},{"id":"spn-65298","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-65299","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/THREE_PROTOCOL_STACK.md"}],"text":"Three-protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-65300","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-65301","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/STACK_COMPLETION.md"}],"text":"Stack status"}]}],"id":"blk-57008","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-57010","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65302","text":"Status: draft v0.1 Owner: runefort.com Date: 2026-04-25 Position: protocol-level. Independent of [&], PULSE, PRISM. May be used by them; does not require them."}]},{"id":"blk-57011","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65303","marks":["bold"],"text":"Related documents:"}]},{"id":"blk-57012","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57014","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65304","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/docs/spec/runefort.core.md"}],"text":"@runefort/core — Reference Web Component Framework v0.1"}]}],"id":"blk-57013","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57016","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65305","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/docs/spec/runefort.dsl.md"}],"text":".rune DSL — v0.1"}]}],"id":"blk-57015","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57018","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65306","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-BUILD-ORDER.md"}],"text":"Interactive Layer — Build Order"}]}],"id":"blk-57017","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57020","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65307","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-1_BYOK.md"}],"text":"RFort-1 — BYOK Modal + OpenRouter Key Storage"}]}],"id":"blk-57019","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57022","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65308","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-2_MCP.md"}],"text":"RFort-2 — MCP Proxy + Client + Connection Panel"}]}],"id":"blk-57021","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57024","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65309","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-3_CHAT.md"}],"text":"RFort-3 — Chat Panel with Fort-Aware Navigation"}]}],"id":"blk-57023","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57026","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65310","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-4_TOKENFLOWS.md"}],"text":"RFort-4 — Token Flow Animations on Edges"}]}],"id":"blk-57025","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57028","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65311","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-5_REPO_IMPORT.md"}],"text":"RFort-5 — Repo Import → Fort Generator"}]}],"id":"blk-57027","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57030","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65312","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-6_WORKSPACES.md"}],"text":"RFort-6 — Workspace Switcher + Supabase Persistence"}]}],"id":"blk-57029","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57031","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65313","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-57032","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65314","text":"0. What this is, in one paragraph"}]},{"id":"blk-57033","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65315","text":"Runefort is a small declarative protocol for describing a "},{"id":"spn-65316","marks":["bold"],"text":"tiled, file-backed UI layout"},{"id":"spn-65317","text":". You declare *rooms* (tiles), *claims* (file-system regions each room owns), *neighbors* (adjacency for navigation), and *state bindings* (how live state colors a tile). A conformant renderer compiles the declaration to a CSS grid, surfaces each claim's content for inline viewing or editing, and overlays live state. The protocol is the contract between the declaration and the renderer. Nothing more."}]},{"id":"blk-57034","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65318","text":"It is not a workforce platform. It is not a supervisor framework. It is not a graph visualization library. It is the "},{"id":"spn-65319","marks":["bold"],"text":"layout language"},{"id":"spn-65320","text":" that those things can be built with."}]},{"id":"blk-57035","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65321","text":"1. Why a protocol (not a library)"}]},{"id":"blk-57036","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57038","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65322","marks":["bold"],"text":"Renderer-portable."},{"id":"spn-65323","text":" The same "},{"id":"spn-65324","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-65325","text":" should render in Elixir/Phoenix, TypeScript/React, or static HTML. The protocol is the only thing they share."}]}],"id":"blk-57037","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57040","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65326","marks":["bold"],"text":"Diffable."},{"id":"spn-65327","text":" Layouts live in version control as text. Reviews become readable. SVG graph layouts cannot do this."}]}],"id":"blk-57039","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57042","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65328","marks":["bold"],"text":"Extensible by composition."},{"id":"spn-65329","text":" Apps add *vocabularies* (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-65330","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor"},{"id":"spn-65331","text":", "},{"id":"spn-65332","marks":["code"],"text":"dashboard"},{"id":"spn-65333","text":", "},{"id":"spn-65334","marks":["code"],"text":"wiki-page"},{"id":"spn-65335","text":") on top of the core primitives. The protocol does not know about supervisors."}]}],"id":"blk-57041","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57044","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65336","marks":["bold"],"text":"No runtime layout engine required."},{"id":"spn-65337","text":" All layout is compile-time deterministic. No d3, no dagre, no jitter."}]}],"id":"blk-57043","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57045","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65338","text":"2. Core primitives"}]},{"id":"blk-57046","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65339","text":"Four primitives. That is the entire vocabulary."}]},{"id":"blk-57047","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65340","text":"2.1 Room"}]},{"id":"blk-57048","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65341","text":"A room is a tile in the grid. It has an id, a position, a size, and arbitrary metadata."}]},{"id":"blk-57049","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"id\": \"memory\",\n  \"position\": [0, 0],\n  \"size\": [3, 2],\n  \"label\": \"memory.ex\",\n  \"meta\": {}\n}"},{"id":"blk-57050","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65342","marks":["code"],"text":"position"},{"id":"spn-65343","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-65344","marks":["code"],"text":"size"},{"id":"spn-65345","text":" are integer cell coordinates in a CSS grid. "},{"id":"spn-65346","marks":["code"],"text":"[0,0]"},{"id":"spn-65347","text":" is top-left. "},{"id":"spn-65348","marks":["code"],"text":"size: [3,2]"},{"id":"spn-65349","text":" means 3 columns wide, 2 rows tall. The renderer is free to choose the cell pixel size; the protocol only specifies cell counts."}]},{"id":"blk-57051","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65350","text":"2.2 Claim"}]},{"id":"blk-57052","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65351","text":"A claim is a file-system region a room \"owns.\" A renderer uses claims to (a) list which files belong to a room and (b) surface those files inline — either as a viewer or an editor — when the user activates the room. Optional behaviors include generating external-editor handoff URLs ("},{"id":"spn-65352","marks":["code"],"text":"vscode://"},{"id":"spn-65353","text":", "},{"id":"spn-65354","marks":["code"],"text":"cursor://"},{"id":"spn-65355","text":", "},{"id":"spn-65356","marks":["code"],"text":"zed://"},{"id":"spn-65357","text":") for users who prefer their own tools."}]},{"id":"blk-57053","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"room\": \"memory\",\n  \"pattern\": \"lib/my_app/memory/**/*.ex\",\n  \"anchor\": \"lib/my_app/forge/memory.ex#L24\"\n}"},{"id":"blk-57054","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65358","marks":["code"],"text":"pattern"},{"id":"spn-65359","text":" is a glob. "},{"id":"spn-65360","marks":["code"],"text":"anchor"},{"id":"spn-65361","text":" is the canonical file the room represents (the one a click on the tile opens)."}]},{"id":"blk-57055","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65362","text":"2.3 Neighbor"}]},{"id":"blk-57056","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65363","text":"A neighbor declares an adjacency between two rooms. Neighbors drive keyboard navigation ("},{"id":"spn-65364","marks":["code"],"text":"h/j/k/l"},{"id":"spn-65365","text":"), focus order, and may be rendered as connecting lines."}]},{"id":"blk-57057","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"from\": \"memory\", \"to\": \"deploy\", \"kind\": \"adjacent\" }"},{"id":"blk-57058","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65366","marks":["code"],"text":"kind"},{"id":"spn-65367","text":" is one of: "},{"id":"spn-65368","marks":["code"],"text":"adjacent"},{"id":"spn-65369","text":" (touching), "},{"id":"spn-65370","marks":["code"],"text":"linked"},{"id":"spn-65371","text":" (logical link, may not be touching), "},{"id":"spn-65372","marks":["code"],"text":"nested"},{"id":"spn-65373","text":" (one contains the other)."}]},{"id":"blk-57059","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65374","text":"2.4 State binding"}]},{"id":"blk-57060","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65375","text":"A state binding tells the renderer how to color a room based on a runtime signal. The protocol defines the *binding*, not the signal source — signals are pushed to the renderer over whatever transport the host app provides (WebSocket, SSE, polling, static)."}]},{"id":"blk-57061","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"room\": \"memory\",\n  \"signal\": \"kappa\",\n  \"thresholds\": [\n    { \"if\": \"< 0.3\", \"class\": \"cold\" },\n    { \"if\": \"< 0.6\", \"class\": \"warm\" },\n    { \"if\": \">= 0.6\", \"class\": \"hot\" }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-57062","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65376","marks":["code"],"text":"class"},{"id":"spn-65377","text":" is a token the renderer maps to CSS. The protocol reserves five canonical classes: "},{"id":"spn-65378","marks":["code"],"text":"cold"},{"id":"spn-65379","text":", "},{"id":"spn-65380","marks":["code"],"text":"warm"},{"id":"spn-65381","text":", "},{"id":"spn-65382","marks":["code"],"text":"hot"},{"id":"spn-65383","text":", "},{"id":"spn-65384","marks":["code"],"text":"fault"},{"id":"spn-65385","text":", "},{"id":"spn-65386","marks":["code"],"text":"idle"},{"id":"spn-65387","text":". Apps may add custom classes — renderers should ignore unknown classes gracefully (treat as "},{"id":"spn-65388","marks":["code"],"text":"cold"},{"id":"spn-65389","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-57063","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65390","text":"3. Document shape"}]},{"id":"blk-57064","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65391","text":"A complete "},{"id":"spn-65392","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-65393","text":" is just an object containing arrays of the four primitives, plus header metadata."}]},{"id":"blk-57065","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"runefort\": \"0.1\",\n  \"title\": \"my_app forge floor\",\n  \"grid\": { \"columns\": 6, \"rows\": 4 },\n  \"rooms\": [ ... ],\n  \"claims\": [ ... ],\n  \"neighbors\": [ ... ],\n  \"state_bindings\": [ ... ],\n  \"vocabulary\": \"core\"\n}"},{"id":"blk-57066","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65394","marks":["code"],"text":"grid.columns"},{"id":"spn-65395","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-65396","marks":["code"],"text":"grid.rows"},{"id":"spn-65397","text":" are the total grid dimensions. "},{"id":"spn-65398","marks":["code"],"text":"vocabulary"},{"id":"spn-65399","text":" is the name of the extension vocabulary in use; "},{"id":"spn-65400","marks":["code"],"text":"\"core\""},{"id":"spn-65401","text":" means no extensions."}]},{"id":"blk-57067","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65402","text":"4. The DSL surface (host-language sugar)"}]},{"id":"blk-57068","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65403","text":"Hosts may expose a DSL that compiles to the JSON above. The DSL is "},{"id":"spn-65404","marks":["bold"],"text":"not normative"},{"id":"spn-65405","text":" — only the JSON is. A reference Elixir DSL:"}]},{"id":"blk-57069","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"defmodule MyApp.Floor do\n  use Runefort.Layout, columns: 6, rows: 4\n\n  room :memory,\n    at: {0, 0}, size: {3, 2},\n    claims: ~r{lib/my_app/memory/},\n    anchor: \"lib/my_app/forge/memory.ex:24\"\n\n  room :deploy,\n    at: {3, 0}, size: {3, 2},\n    claims: ~r{lib/my_app/deploy/}\n\n  neighbors :memory => :deploy\n\n  bind :memory, signal: :kappa,\n    cold: \"< 0.3\", warm: \"< 0.6\", hot: \">= 0.6\"\nend"},{"id":"blk-57070","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65406","text":"A reference TypeScript DSL:"}]},{"id":"blk-57071","kind":"code","language":"ts","text":"const floor = layout({ columns: 6, rows: 4 }, [\n  room(\"memory\", { at: [0,0], size: [3,2], claims: \"lib/my_app/memory/**\" }),\n  room(\"deploy\", { at: [3,0], size: [3,2], claims: \"lib/my_app/deploy/**\" }),\n  neighbor(\"memory\", \"deploy\"),\n  bind(\"memory\", \"kappa\", { cold: \"< 0.3\", warm: \"< 0.6\", hot: \">= 0.6\" }),\n]);"},{"id":"blk-57072","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65407","text":"Both compile to the same JSON. Either is conformant. Neither is privileged."}]},{"id":"blk-57073","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65408","text":"5. Renderer contract"}]},{"id":"blk-57074","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65409","text":"A conformant renderer MUST:"}]},{"id":"blk-57075","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65410","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-65411","marks":["bold"],"text":"Layout."},{"id":"spn-65412","text":" Render rooms in a CSS grid (or visually equivalent) using each room's "},{"id":"spn-65413","marks":["code"],"text":"position"},{"id":"spn-65414","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-65415","marks":["code"],"text":"size"},{"id":"spn-65416","text":". The grid MUST be deterministic — given the same JSON, the rendered DOM order MUST be stable. 2. "},{"id":"spn-65417","marks":["bold"],"text":"Anchors."},{"id":"spn-65418","text":" Resolve each room's "},{"id":"spn-65419","marks":["code"],"text":"anchor"},{"id":"spn-65420","text":" to its content (the file or content region the room represents). Activating a tile MUST surface that content — by default, inline within the host page (viewer or editor). Renderers MAY additionally offer an external-editor handoff URL as a secondary action, but inline surfacing is the canonical behavior. 3. "},{"id":"spn-65421","marks":["bold"],"text":"State classes."},{"id":"spn-65422","text":" Apply CSS classes from "},{"id":"spn-65423","marks":["code"],"text":"state_bindings"},{"id":"spn-65424","text":" to each room's root element. Class names MUST be predictable: "},{"id":"spn-65425","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort-state-cold"},{"id":"spn-65426","text":", "},{"id":"spn-65427","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort-state-hot"},{"id":"spn-65428","text":", etc. 4. "},{"id":"spn-65429","marks":["bold"],"text":"Accessibility."},{"id":"spn-65430","text":" Each room MUST be focusable (keyboard) and have a stable accessible name (the room's "},{"id":"spn-65431","marks":["code"],"text":"label"},{"id":"spn-65432","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-65433","marks":["code"],"text":"id"},{"id":"spn-65434","text":"). 5. "},{"id":"spn-65435","marks":["bold"],"text":"Neighbor navigation."},{"id":"spn-65436","text":" Arrow keys (or "},{"id":"spn-65437","marks":["code"],"text":"h/j/k/l"},{"id":"spn-65438","text":") MUST move focus along "},{"id":"spn-65439","marks":["code"],"text":"neighbor"},{"id":"spn-65440","text":" edges. Renderers MAY also expose mouse navigation; keyboard support is required."}]},{"id":"blk-57076","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65441","text":"A conformant renderer SHOULD:"}]},{"id":"blk-57077","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57079","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65442","text":"Provide an inline editor (not just a read-only viewer) for the focused room's "},{"id":"spn-65443","marks":["code"],"text":"anchor"},{"id":"spn-65444","text":" when the host environment supports text editing."}]}],"id":"blk-57078","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57081","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65445","text":"Highlight neighbor adjacencies on hover/focus."}]}],"id":"blk-57080","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57083","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65446","text":"Re-render on signal change without full reload."}]}],"id":"blk-57082","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57084","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65447","text":"A conformant renderer MAY:"}]},{"id":"blk-57085","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57087","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65448","text":"Add domain-specific vocabularies (see §6)."}]}],"id":"blk-57086","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57089","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65449","text":"Display additional metadata from "},{"id":"spn-65450","marks":["code"],"text":"meta"},{"id":"spn-65451","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-57088","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57091","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65452","text":"Animate state class transitions."}]}],"id":"blk-57090","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57093","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65453","text":"Offer external-editor handoff URLs ("},{"id":"spn-65454","marks":["code"],"text":"vscode://"},{"id":"spn-65455","text":", "},{"id":"spn-65456","marks":["code"],"text":"cursor://"},{"id":"spn-65457","text":", "},{"id":"spn-65458","marks":["code"],"text":"zed://"},{"id":"spn-65459","text":") as a secondary action for users who prefer their own tools. Renderers that run outside the browser (e.g. static-site generators, server-rendered HTML with no JS) MAY treat handoff as their primary surfacing strategy and still claim conformance."}]}],"id":"blk-57092","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57094","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65460","text":"6. Vocabularies (extension points)"}]},{"id":"blk-57095","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65461","text":"The protocol's core knows nothing about supervisors, dashboards, or wikis. Apps declare a *vocabulary* — a named bundle of extra fields on "},{"id":"spn-65462","marks":["code"],"text":"meta"},{"id":"spn-65463","text":", extra signals, and extra state classes."}]},{"id":"blk-57096","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"runefort\": \"0.1\",\n  \"vocabulary\": \"supervisor-floor.v1\",\n  \"rooms\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"memory\",\n      \"position\": [0,0], \"size\": [3,2],\n      \"meta\": {\n        \"supervisor\": {\n          \"autonomy\": \"advise\",\n          \"uptime_seconds\": 957840,\n          \"last_action\": \"consolidated 47 nodes\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-57097","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65464","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-65465","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-65466","text":" vocabulary defines what "},{"id":"spn-65467","marks":["code"],"text":"meta.supervisor"},{"id":"spn-65468","text":" contains. A renderer that doesn't know "},{"id":"spn-65469","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-65470","text":" MUST still render the layout correctly — it just won't display the supervisor-specific overlay. "},{"id":"spn-65471","marks":["bold"],"text":"Vocabulary unknown = degrade, don't fail."}]},{"id":"blk-57098","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65472","text":"Reserved vocabularies (managed by the protocol authors):"}]},{"id":"blk-57099","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57101","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65473","marks":["code"],"text":"core"},{"id":"spn-65474","text":" — the four primitives, no extensions."}]}],"id":"blk-57100","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57103","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65475","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-65476","text":" — for [&]/Runefort supervisor workforce apps."}]}],"id":"blk-57102","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57105","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65477","marks":["code"],"text":"codebase-atlas.v1"},{"id":"spn-65478","text":" — for repository visualization apps."}]}],"id":"blk-57104","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57107","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65479","marks":["code"],"text":"dashboard-grid.v1"},{"id":"spn-65480","text":" — for metric/observability tile dashboards."}]}],"id":"blk-57106","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57108","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65481","text":"Custom vocabularies are namespaced freely ("},{"id":"spn-65482","marks":["code"],"text":"com.example.my-vocab.v1"},{"id":"spn-65483","text":"). The protocol does not require registration."}]},{"id":"blk-57109","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65484","text":"7. Non-goals"}]},{"id":"blk-57110","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65485","text":"Explicit, so the protocol stays small:"}]},{"id":"blk-57111","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57113","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65486","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a graph visualization protocol."},{"id":"spn-65487","text":" Force-directed layouts, dagre, hierarchies — out of scope. Runefort is grids only. If you need a graph, use a graph tool."}]}],"id":"blk-57112","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57115","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65488","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a state-management protocol."},{"id":"spn-65489","text":" How signals are computed, where they live, how they're transported — host's problem."}]}],"id":"blk-57114","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57117","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65490","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a workforce / supervision framework."},{"id":"spn-65491","text":" That's a *vocabulary* ("},{"id":"spn-65492","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-65493","text":"), built on top."}]}],"id":"blk-57116","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57119","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65494","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a presentation framework."},{"id":"spn-65495","text":" No theming spec, no animation spec. CSS is the renderer's job."}]}],"id":"blk-57118","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57121","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65496","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not coupled to [&], PULSE, or PRISM."},{"id":"spn-65497","text":" A "},{"id":"spn-65498","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-65499","text":" describing a recipe app is fully conformant."}]}],"id":"blk-57120","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57122","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65500","text":"8. Versioning"}]},{"id":"blk-57123","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65501","text":"Semver for the protocol itself. The top-level "},{"id":"spn-65502","marks":["code"],"text":"\"runefort\": \"0.1\""},{"id":"spn-65503","text":" field is the protocol version, NOT the renderer version."}]},{"id":"blk-57124","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57126","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65504","marks":["bold"],"text":"Major bump"},{"id":"spn-65505","text":" = breaking JSON shape change."}]}],"id":"blk-57125","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57128","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65506","marks":["bold"],"text":"Minor bump"},{"id":"spn-65507","text":" = additive (new optional fields, new reserved vocabularies, new state classes)."}]}],"id":"blk-57127","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57130","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65508","marks":["bold"],"text":"Patch"},{"id":"spn-65509","text":" = clarification only, no behavior change."}]}],"id":"blk-57129","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57131","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65510","text":"A renderer MUST refuse documents with a major version it does not support. A renderer SHOULD render documents with a higher minor version, ignoring fields it does not recognize."}]},{"id":"blk-57132","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65511","text":"9. Reference framework — "},{"id":"spn-65512","marks":["code"],"text":"@runefort/core"}]},{"id":"blk-57133","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65513","text":"The canonical browser-side reference implementation is "},{"id":"spn-65514","marks":["bold"],"text":"`@runefort/core`"},{"id":"spn-65515","text":": a small set of Web Components ("},{"id":"spn-65516","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-floor>"},{"id":"spn-65517","text":", "},{"id":"spn-65518","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-room>"},{"id":"spn-65519","text":", "},{"id":"spn-65520","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-claim>"},{"id":"spn-65521","text":", "},{"id":"spn-65522","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-link>"},{"id":"spn-65523","text":") implementing this protocol with no framework dependency. ~5KB minified target. Specified in "},{"id":"spn-65524","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.core.md"},{"id":"spn-65525","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-57134","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65526","text":"Why a reference framework, not just a renderer:"}]},{"id":"blk-57135","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57137","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65527","marks":["bold"],"text":"Zero-build adoption."},{"id":"spn-65528","text":" Drop one "},{"id":"spn-65529","marks":["code"],"text":"<script type=\"module\">"},{"id":"spn-65530","text":" tag into any HTML page and the protocol is rendered. No bundler, no npm, no framework."}]}],"id":"blk-57136","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57139","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65531","marks":["bold"],"text":"Universal embedding."},{"id":"spn-65532","text":" Custom Elements work inside React, Vue, Svelte, Solid, Lit, Astro, Phoenix LiveView, Rails view templates, plain HTML. The framework adapters are ~1KB each, not full reimplementations."}]}],"id":"blk-57138","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57141","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65533","marks":["bold"],"text":"Single reactivity story."},{"id":"spn-65534","text":" Property setters on "},{"id":"spn-65535","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-floor>"},{"id":"spn-65536","text":" push signal updates; rooms recompute their state class. No virtual DOM, no opinionated state library — composes with whatever the host app already uses."}]}],"id":"blk-57140","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57142","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65537","text":"Conformant alternatives may exist. "},{"id":"spn-65538","marks":["code"],"text":"@runefort/core"},{"id":"spn-65539","text":" is the reference, not the only option. A pure-Phoenix-LiveView renderer or a server-rendered static-HTML emitter are both valid conformant implementations."}]},{"id":"blk-57143","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65540","text":"9.1 Authoring surfaces"}]},{"id":"blk-57144","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65541","text":"The same protocol is reachable through three authoring surfaces, all equivalent and all round-trippable:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-57146","spans":[{"id":"spn-65542","text":"Surface"}]},{"id":"blk-57147","spans":[{"id":"spn-65543","text":"Format"}]},{"id":"blk-57148","spans":[{"id":"spn-65544","text":"Use case"}]}],"id":"blk-57145","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-57149","spans":[{"id":"spn-65545","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"}]},{"id":"blk-57150","spans":[{"id":"spn-65546","text":"JSON"}]},{"id":"blk-57151","spans":[{"id":"spn-65547","text":"Programmatic generation, tooling integration, canonical persistence"}]}],[{"id":"blk-57152","spans":[{"id":"spn-65548","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-*>"},{"id":"spn-65549","text":" HTML"}]},{"id":"blk-57153","spans":[{"id":"spn-65550","text":"Custom Elements"}]},{"id":"blk-57154","spans":[{"id":"spn-65551","text":"Hand-written pages, embedding inside existing apps"}]}],[{"id":"blk-57155","spans":[{"id":"spn-65552","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-65553","text":" DSL"}]},{"id":"blk-57156","spans":[{"id":"spn-65554","text":"Curly-brace declarative"}]},{"id":"blk-57157","spans":[{"id":"spn-65555","text":"Hand-authored layouts, version control reviewability"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-57158","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65556","text":"The DSL is specified in "},{"id":"spn-65557","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.dsl.md"},{"id":"spn-65558","text":". The CLI converts losslessly between all three."}]},{"id":"blk-57159","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65559","text":"9.2 Planned tree"}]},{"id":"blk-57160","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"runefort/\n  spec/\n    runefort.protocol.md       ← this document\n    runefort.core.md           ← @runefort/core web component spec\n    runefort.dsl.md            ← .rune DSL spec\n    schema.json                ← JSON schema for runefort.json\n  packages/\n    core/                      ← @runefort/core (web components, target ≤5KB)\n    cli/                       ← runefort CLI (compile/fmt/to-rune)\n    react/                     ← @runefort/react adapter (~1KB)\n    vue/                       ← @runefort/vue adapter\n    svelte/                    ← @runefort/svelte adapter\n    liveview/                  ← @runefort/liveview adapter\n  examples/\n    no-framework/              ← raw HTML, proves \"runs anywhere\"\n    supervisor-floor/          ← the [&] use case, proves supervisor-floor.v1\n    codebase-atlas/            ← non-[&], proves genericity\n    dashboard-grid/            ← non-[&], proves genericity"},{"id":"blk-57161","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65560","text":"Two non-[&] examples are required before we cut v0.1 final. Otherwise we're an [&] dashboard with a spec attached."}]},{"id":"blk-57162","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65561","text":"9.3 Build order (v0.1)"}]},{"id":"blk-57163","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65562","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-65563","marks":["code"],"text":"@runefort/core"},{"id":"spn-65564","text":" — the four web components + "},{"id":"spn-65565","marks":["code"],"text":"mount(json)"},{"id":"spn-65566","text":". Smallest meaningful artifact. 2. Playground at runefort.com — live "},{"id":"spn-65567","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-65568","text":" editor → rendered floor. The shareable demo. 3. CLI compile path — "},{"id":"spn-65569","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-65570","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-65571","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-65572","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-65573","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-65574","text":" → static HTML. 4. Adapters — React, then LiveView, then others as demand appears."}]},{"id":"blk-57164","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65575","text":"Adapters wait until non-zero users exist. Shipping all adapters before having users is the wrong direction of optimization."}]},{"id":"blk-57165","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65576","text":"10. Relationship to the [&] stack"}]},{"id":"blk-57166","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65577","text":"Runefort is "},{"id":"spn-65578","marks":["bold"],"text":"independent of"},{"id":"spn-65579","text":" [&]. It does not import, depend on, or require any [&] protocol. However:"}]},{"id":"blk-57167","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57169","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65580","marks":["code"],"text":"[&]"},{"id":"spn-65581","text":" capability descriptors MAY be embedded in "},{"id":"spn-65582","marks":["code"],"text":"meta"},{"id":"spn-65583","text":" under "},{"id":"spn-65584","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-65585","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-57168","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57171","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65586","text":"PULSE manifest phases MAY drive room generation in tooling that bridges PULSE → Runefort."}]}],"id":"blk-57170","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57173","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65587","text":"PRISM scores MAY be a signal source for state bindings."}]}],"id":"blk-57172","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57174","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65588","text":"These are *integration patterns*, not protocol requirements. A Runefort layout that knows nothing about [&] is fully conformant."}]},{"id":"blk-57175","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65589","text":"11. Open questions for v0.2"}]},{"id":"blk-57176","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57178","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65590","marks":["bold"],"text":"Nesting."},{"id":"spn-65591","text":" A room inside a room (zoomable). Worth adding to core, or push to a vocabulary?"}]}],"id":"blk-57177","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57180","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65592","marks":["bold"],"text":"Streaming layout edits."},{"id":"spn-65593","text":" Today the JSON is whole-document. Should there be a patch format?"}]}],"id":"blk-57179","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57182","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65594","marks":["bold"],"text":"Manifest discovery."},{"id":"spn-65595","text":" Does a renderer auto-discover "},{"id":"spn-65596","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-65597","text":" in a repo, or is the path always provided?"}]}],"id":"blk-57181","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57184","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65598","marks":["bold"],"text":"Multiple anchors per room."},{"id":"spn-65599","text":" Today one anchor. Real codebases have N files per logical region."}]}],"id":"blk-57183","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57185","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65600","text":"These are explicitly deferred. v0.1 ships with the four primitives and nothing else."}]},{"id":"blk-57186","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65601","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-57187","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65602","text":"*This spec is the contract. Everything in "},{"id":"spn-65603","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.com/docs/spec/README.md"},{"id":"spn-65604","text":" (the spatial-cognition / dark-factory spec) is now reframed as the "},{"id":"spn-65605","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-65606","text":" vocabulary plus the "},{"id":"spn-65607","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.dark_factory"},{"id":"spn-65608","text":" reference application — both built on top of this protocol.*"}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaiera56p4kitvr6oqodt3gjasowo6on23yl3tutrcqv227xainczd73xq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}